{"id":163,"date":"2026-07-09T14:30:49","date_gmt":"2026-07-09T14:30:49","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/localhost:8181\/four-draft-fixes-for-the-farmhouses-around-indiana-county\/"},"modified":"2026-07-14T19:43:56","modified_gmt":"2026-07-14T19:43:56","slug":"four-draft-fixes-for-the-farmhouses-around-indiana-county","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/four-draft-fixes-for-the-farmhouses-around-indiana-county\/","title":{"rendered":"IUP Student Rentals Kill Furnaces Twice as Fast in Indiana"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover alignfull s-hero-cover\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:2rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:2rem\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim-70 has-background-dim\"><\/span><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-179\" alt=\"furnace basement heating\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/363044088_2d14d4cea7_b.jpg\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/363044088_2d14d4cea7_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/363044088_2d14d4cea7_b-300x200.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/363044088_2d14d4cea7_b-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-cover-is-layout-ff0c90b8 wp-block-cover-is-layout-constrained\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center has-base-color has-text-color s-hero-cover__title wp-block-heading\">Furnaces fail when rentals demand too much<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center s-lead has-base-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">Student rental properties around IUP run furnaces harder and longer than almost any housing stock in western Pennsylvania, yet maintenance schedules often follow semester breaks instead of seasonal need.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Book the Assessment<\/a><\/div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"#content\">Learn More<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"s-trust-bar\"><div class=\"s-trust__item\">15+ Years Serving PA<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Licensed &amp; Insured<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Same-Day Emergency<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Local to Your Area<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Indiana&#039;s Student Rentals Break Furnaces<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Every September brings twenty thousand students back to Indiana, filling rental houses on streets like Philadelphia, Chestnut, and South Sixth where landlords manage portfolios of Victorian conversions and wood-frame doubles built when the town was a mining hub.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">These homes were never designed for the occupancy patterns they see today\u2014eight students in a four-bedroom, thermostats cranked to seventy-five, basement furnaces running full-tilt from October through April with filters that might get changed once if the landlord remembers during a summer turnover. The HVAC challenges in Indiana&#039;s rental corridors are less about equipment age and more about usage intensity combined with neglect.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A furnace that might serve a family of four for fifteen years can be run into the ground in six or seven when it&#039;s heating a house full of students who leave windows cracked, run space heaters in bedrooms, and never think about filter changes because they&#039;re not listed in the lease.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">By January, when heating systems fail, it&#039;s not a surprise\u2014it&#039;s the inevitable outcome of deferred maintenance meeting maximum demand.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-aa34ec83 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:2rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:2rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-cta--inline has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-965f9c1f wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:1.5rem;padding-right:2rem;padding-bottom:1.5rem;padding-left:2rem\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Avoid a mid-winter breakdown in your rental portfolio. <a href=\"\/contact\/\">Get preventive maintenance details<\/a>.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Heat Exchanger Failures: The Cost of Neglect<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Heat exchangers in Indiana&#039;s student rental furnaces fail at rates that would seem impossible in standard residential service because constant cycling and poor airflow create metal fatigue that cracks the steel chambers containing combustion gases. Every time the furnace fires, the heat exchanger expands, then contracts during the off-cycle. In a well-maintained home, this thermal cycling happens six or eight times per day.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a student house where the thermostat cycles twenty or thirty times daily due to open windows, restricted returns, and occupant behavior, the furnace accumulates a full season&#039;s thermal stress in just weeks. When airflow restriction from dirty filters adds to this cycling stress, the heat exchanger runs hotter than designed, accelerating oxidation and making the metal brittle.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cracks typically form at weld seams where stress concentrates, and once a crack develops, combustion gases leak into the airstream circulating through the house. Carbon monoxide risk from cracked heat exchangers is not theoretical in student rentals\u2014it&#039;s a documented hazard in college towns. Preventing failure requires both reducing cycle frequency through proper thermostat programming and maintaining unrestricted airflow through religious filter maintenance.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Monthly filter changes during heating season, annual combustion analysis, and programmable thermostats that reduce cycling frequency are far cheaper than emergency replacements and liability exposure.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/7029986093_4600b63031_b.jpg\" alt=\"furnace basement heating\" class=\"wp-image-178\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/7029986093_4600b63031_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/7029986093_4600b63031_b-300x200.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/7029986093_4600b63031_b-768x512.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;Basement&quot; by Martin Cathrae, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-aa34ec83 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:2rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:2rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-cta--inline has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-965f9c1f wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:1.5rem;padding-right:2rem;padding-bottom:1.5rem;padding-left:2rem\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Learn how preventive maintenance saves money on rental properties. <a href=\"\/contact\/\">Download maintenance checklist<\/a>.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Five Steps to Protect Your Rental Furnace<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-steps\">\n<li>Schedule Monthly Filter Changes \u2014 Replace furnace filters every thirty days during heating season\u2014not quarterly like residential guidelines suggest. High occupancy density and runtime hours triple the dirt load.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Install Programmable Thermostats \u2014 Reduce cycling frequency with temperature locks that prevent overrides. Lockout features prevent students from setting heat to eighty-five or leaving systems running during semester breaks.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Conduct Annual Combustion Analysis \u2014 Test for carbon monoxide in the flue and measure for heat exchanger spillage during off-cycles. This catches problems before they become safety hazards or expensive failures.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Plan Replacements Between Academic Years \u2014 Summer turnover is the only window for major HVAC work. Book equipment and labor in spring for June or July installation before fall occupancy begins.<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Seal Ductwork and Add Insulation \u2014 Summer vacancy allows access to attics and crawl spaces. Sealing duct leaks and adding rim joist insulation improves efficiency and reduces the load on new equipment.<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-cta--card has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-a5a05655 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4rem;padding-right:3.5rem;padding-bottom:4rem;padding-left:3.5rem\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ready to protect your rental properties?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We create summer HVAC plans that fit your portfolio and keep tenants warm through finals week without mid-winter surprises.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Start Your Plan \/rental-assessment<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Services Built for Rental Property Challenges<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Student housing demands a different HVAC approach than single-family residential service. Our rental-focused maintenance and replacement protocols account for usage intensity, budget constraints, and seasonal occupancy patterns that make standard service intervals irrelevant.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-icon-list\">\n<li>Emergency furnace repair and replacement when systems fail during occupancy<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Planned replacement scheduling during summer vacancy windows with advance booking<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Filter service and maintenance programs that keep pace with high-occupancy demand<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Thermostat programming and lockout installation for student tenant oversight<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Combustion safety testing and heat exchanger assessment before mid-season failures<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Ductwork sealing and insulation upgrades during vacant periods between leases<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Load calculations for converted Victorian and multi-unit properties with zoning mismatches<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text\" style=\"grid-template-columns:50% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-thermostat-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"thermostat - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1479\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-thermostat-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-thermostat-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-thermostat-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-thermostat-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Thermostat Strategy for Student Rentals<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Programmable and smart thermostats offer property owners a way to reduce heating costs without sacrificing comfort, but only if they&#039;re installed with lockout features preventing tenant overrides. The most effective strategy for Indiana rental properties is to install thermostats with configurable temperature ranges that maintain minimum winter temperatures around sixty-two degrees when units are unoccupied during breaks, then allow tenant control within a limited range during occupancy.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Smart thermostats with geofencing can automatically adjust setpoints when residents leave for classes, reducing runtime during the day when solar gain provides passive heating. Over a full heating season, these small adjustments can reduce furnace runtime by fifteen to twenty percent without affecting perceived comfort.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For landlords managing multiple properties, cloud-based systems offer visibility into heating patterns across the portfolio, flagging units running excessive hours due to equipment problems, insulation deficiencies, or tenant behavior that needs addressing. The key to success is setting expectations clearly in leases about temperature ranges and prohibited practices like opening windows to cool down instead of adjusting the thermostat.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When students understand that excessive heating costs will be deducted from deposits, and when thermostats provide clear feedback about settings and costs, behavior changes become possible.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-aa34ec83 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:2rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:2rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-cta--inline has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-965f9c1f wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:1.5rem;padding-right:2rem;padding-bottom:1.5rem;padding-left:2rem\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Tenants respect rules when they understand the costs. <a href=\"\/contact\/\">See thermostat control options<\/a>.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Summer Planning Matters in Indiana<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-indent has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The summer turnover window between spring move-out and fall lease start is the only realistic time for major HVAC work in Indiana student rentals, but it&#039;s also when every other landlord tries to schedule the same contractors for the same narrow window. Properties that wait until a furnace fails in March hope to replace it before August but compete for contractor attention with dozens of other emergencies.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Smart property owners identify failing systems during winter inspections, order replacement equipment in early spring when manufacturers offer pre-season pricing, and schedule installation in June or July when labor is available and work proceeds without rushing or weather complications. Replacement planning should account for the usage intensity these systems will face.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Standard eighty-percent efficiency furnaces work, but commercial-grade or modulating units handle frequent cycling better and offer finer temperature control that reduces cycling frequency. Variable-speed blowers reduce electrical consumption and provide quieter operation in houses with thin walls between units. High-efficiency filters with pleated media last longer and provide better air quality in high-occupancy homes.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Indiana Landlords Choose Keystone Comfort<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-feature-row is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg\" alt=\"hvac technician repair\" class=\"wp-image-188\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;AC Service&quot; by SuperTech HVAC Services, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Rental Portfolio Expertise<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We manage HVAC for properties across South Sixth, Philadelphia, and Chestnut\u2014we know what breaks and when.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1475\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Summer-Window Scheduling<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We book replacement and upgrade work months in advance and can complete projects during vacant periods between leases.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1476\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Preventive Maintenance Programs<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Fixed-schedule filter changes, combustion analysis, and system inspections prevent emergency calls during occupancy.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1755\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Transparent Tenant Communication<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We help landlords explain HVAC expectations and costs in lease agreements so tenants understand the system&#039;s limitations.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1756\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Load Calculations for Conversions<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Victorian houses split into apartments and multi-unit rentals need custom analysis\u2014we provide sizing recommendations based on actual occupancy.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-pills s-pills--glass\">\n<li>Monthly filter changes in rentals (not quarterly)<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Heat exchanger lifespan: 8\u201312 years under rental-intensity use<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Carbon monoxide testing: annual requirement for cracked-heat-exchanger diagnosis<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Summer replacement window: only realistic time for major work<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Thermostat lockouts: prevent tenant overrides and excessive cycling<\/li>\n\n\n<li>IUP student housing: 20,000 occupants plus peak demand in January<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Common HVAC Questions from Indiana Property Owners<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-accordion s-accordion--bordered has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-1583283a wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>How often should furnace filters be changed in student rental properties?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Monthly during heating season is the minimum for high-occupancy student rentals, and every three weeks is better if occupancy exceeds six people. Standard residential guidance of quarterly changes does not apply when occupancy density and runtime hours are three or four times higher than design assumptions.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Can I charge tenants for excessive heating costs in Indiana rental properties?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Pennsylvania law allows utility cost pass-through if specified in the lease before occupancy begins. Many landlords include heating cost caps or require tenants to maintain thermostats within specified ranges, with overages billed separately. Consult local rental ordinances and fair housing rules before implementing cost-sharing arrangements.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>What&#039;s the typical lifespan of a furnace in a student rental compared to single-family use?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Eight to twelve years is realistic for rental property furnaces versus fifteen to twenty years in single-family homes, assuming equivalent equipment quality. The higher cycle count and deferred maintenance in rentals accelerate wear on blower motors, heat exchangers, and gas valves that would last much longer in lower-intensity applications.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Why does my Philadelphia Street rowhouse run ten degrees colder upstairs every winter?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Converted Victorian homes often have undersized ductwork from the 1940s paired with oversized equipment, creating distribution imbalances. A proper load calculation and ductwork upgrade will show exactly why upper floors stay cold and how to fix it.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>When is the best time to replace my rental property furnace?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">June through August, during the summer turnover window when units are vacant. Planning in spring allows you to order equipment at pre-season pricing and secure contractor availability before fall occupancy begins.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Our Work in Your Neighborhood<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery alignwide has-nested-images columns-3 is-cropped s-gallery wp-block-gallery-2 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" data-id=\"188\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg\" alt=\"hvac technician repair\" class=\"wp-image-188\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;AC Service&quot; by SuperTech HVAC Services, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img lo